---
description: scout -> planner -> worker implementation workflow
---

Use a chain of subagents to implement: <request>

1. Run the `scout` agent to find everything relevant to <request>. Ask for
   compressed findings with file paths and line ranges.
2. Pass those findings to the `planner` agent and ask for a concrete,
   ordered plan.
3. Pass the plan to a `worker` agent and have it implement the plan exactly.

Report the final result and a short summary of what changed. If any step
fails, stop and report which step failed and why.

When invoking project-local agents from a trusted project, pass
`confirmProjectAgents: false` to skip the repeat confirmation prompt.
